    "content" : "Here&#39;s the electronics of my latest project -- a automatic garden waterer. I re-purposed the PCB from my MSP430 Reaction Game project (<a href=\"http://tinkeringetc.blogspot.com/p/msp430-reaction-game.html\" class=\"ot-anchor\">http://tinkeringetc.blogspot.com/p/msp430-reaction-game.html</a>). This is the front panel of an electrical gang box. The dial will adjust how much time to water the plants and then the MSP430 will switch on a relay that will open up a valve for the water to flow. I hope to finish up the electrical aspect of it tomorrow, then I only need to modify the original program to get it to work as I intended. Stay tuned!",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "Here's the electronics of my latest project -- a automatic garden waterer. I re-purposed the PCB from my MSP430 Reaction Game project (http://tinkeringetc.blogspot.com/p/msp430-reaction-game.html). This is the front panel of an electrical gang box. The dial will adjust how much time to water the plants and then the MSP430 will switch on a relay that will open up a valve for the water to flow. I hope to finish up the electrical aspect of it tomorrow, then I only need to modify the original program to get it to work as I intended. Stay tuned!",
